   loaded and nothing is sent until the reader clicks. New pages: #/privacy (no cookies, analytics or ads; what local
   storage keeps) and #/share (one-line description, link code, share picture, feed).
+
+## v5.26: 60 origin stories, one start-page grid, retry on a dropped connection, no dead end on "How it's made"
+- `pipeline/origin_stories.json`: 27 stories drafted by Gemini (batches 5 and 6) were checked against their sources before going in (full text
+  from NCBI eutils `efetch` or Europe PMC, the abstract where the publisher withholds the text, NobelPrize.org); most were corrected and five
+  cited papers were about something else, so they were dropped. A story may carry its own `checked` date, which `build_catalogue.py` keeps.
+  Nothing is held back any more (cisplatin has a readable source; artemisinin's story is on artesunate's page).
+- Start page (`js/app.js` `start()`): the six roles in one `.lens-grid` under "How are you exploring today?" (Dmitry's Option 2); the switcher
+  reads "Reference →" / "← Explore". Cards use `--paper`, so they follow dark mode.
+- `data.getJSON` tries once more after 400 ms when `fetch` itself fails, and marks the error `network`; the router then shows
+  "Connection interrupted" with a Try again button. A missing file or bad JSON still shows "We couldn't find that page".
+- Simple "How it's made" page of a medicine without a discovery story: "What the records say" (oldest date by region and what it is, first US
+  generic, family from `family_trees.json`, WHO list), built in `explore.js` from fields the page already has. Gemini's
+  `build_drug_histories.py` / `fetch_drug_histories.py` were not taken: they copied the same dates into every drug file with new wording
+  (some of it wrong, e.g. generic counts "across N sponsors" used all sponsors) and added Europe PMC papers matched only by title words as sources.
+- `pipeline/run_all.sh`: the PubChem cross-check now runs before `fetch_extra_chembl.py` and is skipped only when `raw/pubchem.json` has the
+  `crosscheck` marker. Before, the top-up written by `fetch_extra_chembl.py` made a fresh build skip the cross-check entirely, and every page
+  said "Not found in PubChem by InChIKey".
+- `config/site.json`: Google Search Console verification token.
